    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="59">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 59</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa on ciningces hirede gefeohte, þolige þæs lifes, butan se cingc him gearian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa on cynincges hirde feohte, þolige þæs lifes, buton him se cynincg gearian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="59" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in familia (id est in curia) regis pugnet, uitę suę reus sit, nisi rex ei misereri uelit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="59" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="204" ed="#robertson"/>Be ðam þe on cynincges hirde feohteð. Gyf hwa on kynincges hirede gefeohte, ðolie ðæs liues, buton him se kynincg geárian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="284" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif hwa on ciningces hirede gefeohte, þolige þæs lifes butan se cingc him gearian wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von dem, der am Königshofe ficht. B) Wenn einer am Königshofe ficht, verliere er das Leben, ausser wenn der König ihm Gnade gewähren will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of him who fights at the king's court. B) If anyone fights at the king's court, let him lose his life, unless the king will grant him mercy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="205" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning those who fight at the king's Court. If anyone fights at the king's Court, he shall lose his life, unless the king is willing to pardon him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="470" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone fight in the king’s court, he is to forfeit his life, unless the king wishes to spare him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="285" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone fights within the king’s household, he shall lose his life unless the king is willing to show mercy to him.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="350"><ref target="clause:Af_7">Af 7</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 7</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="353"><label>rephrases</label> <ref target="clause:Af_7">Af 7</ref> <quote>Likewise, II 57, 59: rephrased Af 4 – 4:2, 7 respectively</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_7">Af 7</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 59: Af 7</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="470"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_7">Af 7</ref> <quote>cf. Alfred 7</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="367"><label>likely reference to</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_6">Ine 6</ref> <quote>Likely references include [...] ii Cnut §59 (Ine §6)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Af 7.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">cf. Alfred 7</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Be ðam þe on cynincges hirde feohteð</note>
      </div>
